udio UI provides results visualization and zero-code interaction with the Agent.\nL224: \nL225: This repository is the main entry point for ServingStudio, with compatible component revisions and shared commands to build and run them.\nL226: ## 🎬 Demo\nL227: \nL228: Explore the cite97†product introduction†syfi-servingstudio.github.io for workflows and performance case studies.\nL229: \nL230: ## 📣 News\nL231: \nL232:   * September 2026 · Introducing ServingStudio: a simulator, an Agent, and an interactive analysis application for LLM serving research and development.\nL233: ## 💡 Close the loop on serving performance\nL234: \nL235: ServingStudio connects simulation and implementation in one evidence-driven loop:\nL236: Step  | Stage  | What happens\nL237: --- | --- | ---\nL238: 1  | Set the target and baseline  | Define the model, request mix, hardware, and performance target, then measure the current deployment to establish a baseline.\nL239: 2  | Explore in simulation  | Sweep serving configurations and inspect predicted operation costs to select one change worth testing.\nL240: 3  | Implement one change  | Apply the selected change to vLLM or SGLang, from a kernel optimization to a new model implementation; pass correctness checks before measuring performance.\nL241: 4  | Profile the change  | Capture a GPU trace of the modified implementation and break down execution time across kernels, communication, and idle gaps.\nL343: ## About\nL344: \nL345: No description, website, or topics provided.\nL346: \nL347: ### Resources\nL348: \nL349: cite71†Readme L350: \nL351: Cite this repository\nL352: \nL353: cite72†Activity L354: \nL355: cite73†Custom properties L356: \nL357: ### Stars\nL358: \nL359: 11 stars\nL360: \nL361: ### Watchers\nL362: \nL363: 1 watching\nL364: \nL365: ### Forks\nL366: \nL367: cite74†3 forks L368: \nL369: cite75†Report repository L370: \nL371: ## Releases\nL372: \nL373: ## Packages\nL374: \nL375: ## Contributors\nL376: \nL377: ## Lan