aluations showed that KREX delivers up to $3.4\\times$ the throughput of command-granular exclusivity at a negligible timing inflation, preserving the relative performance signals that guide the agent’s search.\nL254: ## Acknowledgments\nL255: \nL256: The authors used an AI assistant for prose editing. All technical content was authored and verified by the human authors.\nL257: ## References\nL258:   * Adams et al. (2019) A. Adams, K. Ma, L. Anderson, R. Baghdadi, T. Li, M. Gharbi, B. Steiner, S. Johnson, K. Fatahalian, F. Durand, and J. Ragan-Kelley Learning to optimize Halide with tree search and random programs. ACM Transactions on Graphics 38 (4), pp. 1–12. External Links: cite100†Document†dx.doi.org Cited by: cite101†§1 .\nL259:   * Alibaba Group (2026a) Alibaba Group AKA: atrex kernel agent. Note: cite102†https://github.com/alibaba/atrex-kernel-agent†github.com Cited by: cite103†§1 , cite104†§2.2 , cite105†§6.1 .\nL260:   * Alibaba Group (2026b) Alibaba Group Atrex-bench: end-to-end operator generation benchmark for multiple DSLs. Note: cite106†https://github.com/alibaba/atrex-bench†github.com Cited by: cite105†§6.1 .\nL261:   * AMD-AGI (2025) AMD-AGI GEAK: generating efficient AI-centric kernels. Note: cite107†https://github.com/AMD-AGI/GEAK†github.com Cited by: cite105†§6.1 .\nL262:   * Bai et al. (2020) Z. Bai, Z. Zhang, Y. Zhu, and X. Jin PipeSwitch: fast pipelined context switching for deep learning applications. In 14th USENIX Symposium on Operating Systems Design and Implementation (OSDI 20), pp. 499–514. External Links: cite108†Link†www.usenix.org Cited by: cite109†§8 .\nL263:   * Cao et al. (1994) P. Cao, E. W. Felten, and K. Li Implementation and performance of application-controlled file caching. In Proceedings of the 1st USENIX Symposium on Operating Systems Design and Implementation (OSDI), External Links: cite110†Link†www.usenix.org Cited by: cite111†§4.1 .\nL264:   * Chen et al. (2018a) T. Chen, T. Morea